{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01XfgwvZdRJG8kWRXjMLKVYU","type":"tool_result","content":"# Voyager 2 Key Facts\n\n**Launch:** \"Aug. 20, 1977 / 14:29:44 UT\" from \"Cape Canaveral, Fla. / Launch Complex 41\"\n\n**Uranus Flyby:** The spacecraft reached Uranus on January 24, 1986, approaching within \"about 50,640 miles (81,500 kilometers)\" of the planet's cloud tops.\n\n**Neptune Flyby:** Voyager 2 encountered Neptune on August 25, 1989, passing \"about 2,980 miles (4,800 kilometers) over the cloud tops\" at its closest point.\n\n**Discoveries at Neptune:** The mission revealed \"six new moons (Proteus, Larissa, Despina, Galatea, Thalassa, and Naiad) and four new rings\" around the distant giant planet."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8c0f2705-b4d3-4236-acdf-26fd44f453d1","uuid":"5e8cbf70-b33e-41e7-a65f-ae59c6727a04","timestamp":"2026-09-26T16:57:21.179Z","tool_use_result":{"bytes":327590,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"# Voyager 2 Key Facts\n\n**Launch:** \"Aug. 20, 1977 / 14:29:44 UT\" from \"Cape Canaveral, Fla. / Launch Complex 41\"\n\n**Uranus Flyby:** The spacecraft reached Uranus on January 24, 1986, approaching within \"about 50,640 miles (81,500 kilometers)\" of the planet's cloud tops.\n\n**Neptune Flyby:** Voyager 2 encountered Neptune on August 25, 1989, passing \"about 2,980 miles (4,800 kilometers) over the cloud tops\" at its closest point.\n\n**Discoveries at Neptune:** The mission revealed \"six new moons (Proteus, Larissa, Despina, Galatea, Thalassa, and Naiad) and four new rings\" around the distant giant planet.","durationMs":4601,"url":"<redacted>
